===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|lighten|alt1=light(e)n|-ing}}.  {{doublet|en|lightening}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlaɪt.nɪŋ/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlaɪt.nɪŋ/|[ˈlʌɪ̯ʔ.nɪŋ]|[ˈlɐɪ̯ʔ.nɪŋ]|a=GenAm}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-lightning.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪtnɪŋ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A [[flash]] of [[light]] produced by short-duration, high-voltage [[discharge]] of [[electricity]] within a [[cloud]], between clouds, or between a cloud and the earth.<!--which heats the air and typically causes thunder-->
#: {{ux|en|Although we did not see the '''lightning''', we did hear the thunder.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Job|38|35||Canst thou send '''lightnings''', that they may go, and say unto thee, Here we are?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1901|author=E. L. Morris|title=The Child's Eden|page=16| passage=It was the thought of hot July and August days, when the clouds piled up like woolly mountains, and '''lightnings''' streaked the sky.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Kathy Clark|title=Stand By Your Man|page=280| passage=Manny drove a few miles per hour under the speed limit, entranced by the awesome display of '''lightning''' streaking out of the clouds toward earth.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|title=Genshin Impact|publisher=miHoYo| date=2021-10-13| version=2.2| system=iOS, Android, Windows, PS4| level=The Sun-Wheel and Mt. Kanna| passage="Ruu": The adults in the village all said that children like me could calm the '''lightning''' and turn the storms into timely rain.}}
# A discharge of this kind.
#: {{ux|en|The '''lightning''' was hot enough to melt the sand.}}
#: {{ux|en|That tree was hit by '''lightning'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=46|passage=''Auster'' and ''Aquilon'' with winged Steeds<br>All ſweating, tilt about the watery heauens,<br>With ſhiuering ſpeares enforcing thunderclaps,<br>And from their ſhields ſtrike flames of '''lightening'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1881|author=Daniel Pierce Thompson|title=The Green Mountain Boys| page=281| passage=The rain at length ceased; and the '''lightnings''', as they played along the black parapet of clouds, that lay piled in the east, shone with less dazzling fierceness, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Anything that moves very fast.
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Land That Time Forgot||V|passage=Nobs, though, was '''lightning''' by comparison with the slow thinking beast and dodged his opponent's thrust with ease. Then he raced to the rear of the tremendous thing and seized it by the tail.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|slang}} {{1|gin}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Jake Arnott|title=The Fatal Tree
|passage=I took some gin but it did little to calm my mood. {{...}} 'Come now, Bess,' she entreated, and poured another glass of '''lightning'''. 'Tell your old mother everything.' I took a gulp of the spirit, then babbled all, showing her the loot now in my possession.}}
# {{obsolete form of|en|lightening}}<ref>{{R:Webster 1913}}</ref>

